I've been playing NH3.0 PL9 on a Mac Plus, and I have a couple of
small bug reports and a lot of questions.

Bugs: 
-When I open a saved game by double-clicking on it, the character is
renamed to the default character name.
-I cannot use the miniWRITER DA to log my progress, because Nethack
reads the letters I type as commands.

Troll SPOILER below!

-In 2.3, a troll either left a corpse or an item. Now, they seem to
always leave corpses, and sometimes also items. This lends itself to a
certain amount of abuse, since you can get five or six items from the
same ressuscitating troll if you are patient (I just love those throne
rooms with 5 or 6 Ts in them!).

Questions ,observations and a few SPOILERS:

-There was some talk about full moons decreasing your luck when you
save/restore. Well, I have been saving/restoring during a new moon, and
I think that my luck increases! I just got a wish from a throne and a
peek at it a while ago in wizard mode showed it to be 10. Pretty
significant, especially since I have no luckstone.

-Does anybody know a good way of getting rid of gelatinous cubes? If you
hit them they paralyze and kill you, so I usually wait till I find a
cockatrice corpse and then stone them, but they are a nuisance and could
be dangerous.

-I'm having a pretty good game so far (AC-12, gauntlets of power, I made
Orcrist, got Giantslayer and Dragonbane from Thoth and Stormbringer
from that wish).  In my opinion the most important item in the game is the
lowly *blindfold*: I cannot count the number of times my weapon, armor,
or life have been saved by applying it every twenty or so turns and using 
the / key. The next best thing, by the way, is that wonderful unicorn horn
(tainted meat, here I come!).

-About those gauntlets of power: I now have strength 18/46 (thank you
Giantslayer), and I cannot lift even a single gem more by putting my
gauntlets on! Pretty wimpy power, I'd say!! On the other hand, they do
seem to increase my damage, but that's just an impression. Does anyone
know the truth?

-A small spoiler about helms from from wizard mode: 
It seems that, for a neutral character, a -1 helm of opposite alignment
makes me chaotic, while a blessed +1 helm makes me lawful. 

-And a question from wizard mode also: I kept sacrificing titan corpses
to Ptah but never got Excalibur. I got everything else including
Mjollnir, then scarificed another 30 corpses with 0 results. Why? Can
you only get Excalibur from the Lady and not from your god?

Well, back to the dungeon, I'm still missing cold, sleep and
disintegration resistance as well as a few items (such as that
luckstone, tinning kit and wand of polymorph!)

And by the way, the game is wonderful and runs just great on my lowly
Mac Plus (even though I can usually tell when a band of orcs is coming
because everything slows down).
